    "text": "Tax-deductibility of donations to \"charities\" should be abolished. They're subsidized by all taxpayers & citizens through the deduction, and through inflation due to money printing to cover deficits.\ne.g. If someone in a 50% tax bracket donates $1000, it only costs them $500. WE pay the other $500 even if we oppose the charity.\nAmong the worst offenders, eco-communist land trusts like The Nature Conservancy. They use our money to buy up (or receive) private land and then keep everyone but themselves off of it, or only on it with their permission under their eco-commie rules, slashing the supply of private land, jacking up land & housing cost and homelessness.\nIf a charity's righteous, people should be willing to donate with their own money, not everyone else's.",
